0,-1)$ but the horizontal asymptote stays at $y=0.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006735/assets/844a32e9d3640f9244b867c7411241171902c848defa0bf653b3820c3850238d.png)\n\n \n\n- Then, vertically shift it by $5$ units up to give $y=-{e}^{x}+5.$ The point $(0,-1)$ moves to $(0,4)$ and the horizontal asymptote moves from from $y=0$ to $y=5.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006735/assets/c4cd8597702179629617890fce31272aa447a3227b74231e787a61eb4e770589.png)" 13194139534435 true] [17592186288092 1000 #edb/ref 17592186288093 13194139534435 true] [17592186288092 1000 #edb/ref 17592186288094 13194139534435 true] [17592186288092 1000 #edb/ref 17592186288095 13194139534435 true] [17592186288092 1000 #edb/ref 17592186288096 13194139534435 true] [17592186288092 1000 #edb/ref 17592186288097 13194139534435 true] [17592186288092 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534435 true] [17592186288092 1041 "selection" 13194139534435 true] [17592186288092 1104 #edb/ref 17592186288096 13194139534435 true] [17592186288092 1110 #uuid "fe71d644-f1b1-570b-9374-0a70548f9d24" 13194139534435 true] [17592186288093 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006735/assets/2ebda1ba75caec9c62a9758696d2c4c45b452c29088e3811edfacd03acf3cd70.png" 13194139534435 true] [17592186288093 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534435 true] [17592186288093 1111 #uuid "1a00f90a-ee29-5b3c-816d-2dc5523f4511" 13194139534435 true] [17592186288094 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006735/assets/28e24035715baa30e89392408359033dc402264c0fdcdc5968addaa615aedf81.png" 13194139534435 true] [17592186288094 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534435 true] [17592186288094 1111 #uuid "fe91b53f-e376-5bfd-ae51-44942ea6aeb7" 13194139534435 true] [17592186288095 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006735/assets/be39498e5ad2c3148b254844722af707d721d7447a393a2341c6c0f6690c603e.png" 13194139534435 true] [17592186288095 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534435 true] [17592186288095 1111 #uuid "8bd88fe1-3e9d-52e3-b5bd-ca9c372b50b8" 13194139534435 true] [17592186288096 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006735/assets/b83ad0f69e6d4a61227c77b3dede3632accdceaa59c1bf63da8ca8bc3fe5a7f9.png" 13194139534435 true] [17592186288096 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534435 true] [17592186288096 1111 #uuid "c5487b96-5648-53cd-8412-d6f4288a834b" 13194139534435 true] [17592186288097 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006735/assets/01cc790392c233d00b4ab30e939230a0e7ac31708a0f568557a3e36e2cf04d67.png" 13194139534435 true] [17592186288097 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534435 true] [17592186288097 1111 #uuid "fd94c884-7b43-50e8-947a-0fc7f75f7998" 13194139534435 true] [17592186288098 1017 #edb/ref 17592186288099 13194139534435 true] [17592186288098 1089 "q-340099" 13194139534435 true] [17592186288098 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534435 true] [17592186288098 1100 "Given the function  $y=2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+{e}^{x}$, find the instantaneous rate of change at $x=1.$ Do not round the answer.\n\nThe instantaneous rate of change at $x=1$ is\n{{field-1}}." 13194139534435 true] [17592186288098 1113 #uuid "4e3f0e53-ded2-5798-9bc9-a98acc8b7d0e" 13194139534435 true] [17592186288098 1145 "To find the instantaneous rate of change at a given point, we have to find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ at that point.\n\nTaking the derivative, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+{e}^{x}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{x}+{e}^{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the instantaneous rate of change at $x=1$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=1} & ={(\\frac{2}{x}+{e}^{x})|}_{x=1} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{1}+{e}^{1} \\\\  & =2+e\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534435 true] [17592186288099 1000 #edb/ref 17592186288100 13194139534435 true] [17592186288099 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534435 true] [17592186288099 1041 "field-1" 13194139534435 true] [17592186288099 1104 #edb/ref 17592186288100 13194139534435 true] [17592186288099 1110 #uuid "bff671db-ed68-5416-b881-dba2591e1dc2" 13194139534435 true] [17592186288100 1034 "2+e" 13194139534435 true] [17592186288100 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534435 true] [17592186288100 1111 #uuid "f89affeb-c9cb-51a3-a416-c44398f9915a" 13194139534435 true] [17592186288101 1017 #edb/ref 17592186288102 13194139534435 true] [17592186288101 1089 "q-35081" 13194139534435 true] [17592186288101 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534435 true] [17592186288101 1100 "Rewrite $3{q}^{2}-9q+15$ by completing the square." 13194139534435 true] [17592186288101 1113 #uuid "59a40bee-f512-5946-aafb-1fc0d88ab700" 13194139534435 true] [17592186288101 1145 "Notice that the leading coefficient is $3.$ So, we take out a factor of $3$ from the entire expression:\n\n$$\n3({q}^{2}-3q+5)\n$$\n\nLet's now complete the square for the expression inside the parentheses:\n\n$$\n{q}^{2}-3q+5\n$$\n\nFirst, we rewrite the coefficient of the linear term as a product with $2$ as a factor:\n\n$$\n{q}^{2}-2\\cdot \\frac{3}{2}\\cdot q+5\n$$\n\nThen, we *add* and *then subtract* ${(\\frac{3}{2})}^{2},$ writing the constant term $5$ last:\n\n$$\n{{q}^{2}-2\\cdot \\frac{3}{2}\\cdot q+{(\\frac{3}{2})}^{2}}_{⏟}-{(\\frac{3}{2})}^{2}+5\n$$\n\nThe first three terms form a perfect square, which we factor as follows:\n\n$$\n{(q-\\frac{3}{2})}^{2}-{(\\frac{3}{2})}^{2}+5\n$$\n\nEvaluating the last two terms, we get\n\n$$\n{(q-\\frac{3}{2})}^{2}+\\frac{11}{4}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute this result back into our original expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3({q}^{2}-3q+5) & =3({(q-\\frac{3}{2})}^{2}+\\frac{11}{4}) \\\\  & =3{(q-\\frac{3}{2})}^{2}+3\\cdot \\frac{11}{4} \\\\  & =3{(q-\\frac{3}{2})}^{2}+\\frac{33}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534435 true] [17592186288102 1000 #edb/ref 17592186288103 13194139534435 true] [17592186288102 1000 #edb/ref 17592186288104 13194139534435 true] [17592186288102 1000 #edb/ref 17592186288105 13194139534435 true] [17592186288102 1000 #edb/ref 17592186288106 13194139534435 true] [17592186288102 1000 #edb/ref 17592186288107 13194139534435 true] [17592186288102 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534435 true] [17592186288102 1041 "selection" 13194139534435 true] [17592186288102 1104 #edb/ref 17592186288106 13194139534435 true] [17592186288102 1110 #uuid "2a22e649-9faf-54c1-94a0-495cebfb7361" 13194139534435 true] [17592186288103 1034 "3{(q-\\frac{3}{2})}^{2}+\\frac{9}{2}" 13194139534435 true] [17592186288103 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534435 true] [17592186288103 1111 #uuid "3619cf01-ea91-57d9-bbd0-7d43b8632f36" 13194139534435 true] [17592186288104 1034 "3{(q-3)}^{2}+3" 13194139534435 true] [17592186288104 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534435 true] [17592186288104 1111 #uuid "3b1b2f61-ddae-55c2-b617-4d3ee295e617" 13194139534435 true] [17592186288105 1034 "3{(q-3)}^{2}-12" 13194139534435 true] [17592186288105 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534435 true] [17592186288105 1111 #uuid "d39c0330-fee5-507e-bdd1-da77637148f3" 13194139534435 true] [17592186288106 1034 "3{(q-\\frac{3}{2})}^{2}+\\frac{33}{4}" 13194139534435 true] [17592186288106 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534435 true] [17592186288106 1111 #uuid "c5aa5192-d570-586c-98a6-48160e3e2557" 13194139534435 true] [17592186288107 1034 "3{(q-\\frac{3}{2})}^{2}+\\frac{11}{4}" 13194139534435 true] [17592186288107 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534435 true] [17592186288107 1111 #uuid "699ce76e-3bd4-59ea-b31c-ae1693a193f1" 13194139534435 true] [17592186288108 1017 #edb/ref 17592186288109 13194139534435 true] [17592186288108 1089 "q-59454" 13194139534435 true] [17592186288108 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534435 true] [17592186288108 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006735/assets/3303e36eb359692802a1c2184a2c54591f0b5de05853691841191a65689e8735.png)\n\nThe speed-time graph represents the motion of an object. Calculate the deceleration of the object." 13194139534435 true] [17592186288108 1113 #uuid "c6acbde6-eb5a-5b0e-a420-9d6912e79be1" 13194139534435 true] [17592186288108 1145 "The object is decelerating when its acceleration is negative. In a speed-time graph, the acceleration is given by the slope of the line.\n\nThe line passes through the points $(30,10)$ and $(50,5),$ so its slope is:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{5\\text{ m/s}-10\\text{ m/s}}{50\\text{ s}-30\\text{ s}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{5\\text{ m/s}}{20\\text{ s}} \\\\  & =-0.25\\,\\frac{\\text{m}}{{\\text{s}}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the acceleration of the object is $-0.25\\,\\text{m}/{\\text{s}}^{2},$ which means that the deceleration of the object is $0.25\\,\\text{m}/{\\text{s}}^{2}.$" 13194139534435 true] [17592186288109 1000 #edb/ref 17592186288110 13194139534435 true] [17592186288109 1000 #edb/ref 17592186288111 13194139534435 true] [17592186288109 1000 #edb/ref 17592186288112 13194139534435 true] [17592186288109 1000 #edb/ref 17592186288113 13194139534435 true] [17592186288109 1000 #edb/ref 17592186288114 13194139534435 true] [17592186288109 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534435 true] [17592186288109 1041 "selection" 13194139534435 true] [17592186288109 1104 #edb/ref 17592186288114 13194139534435 true] [17592186288109 1110 #uuid "85ecdabf-507b-527a-9d1a-49143430ec08" 13194139534435 true] [17592186288110 1034 "0.4\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}" 13194139534435 true] [17592186288110 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534435 true] [17592186288110 1111 #uuid "91605a00-67bd-5464-bc69-6904e8cd248c" 13194139534435 true] [17592186288111 1034 "5\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}" 13194139534435 true] [17592186288111 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534435 true] [17592186288111 1111 #uuid "8731f1cb-d519-5ea9-aec6-2e6f79d56fb0" 13194139534435 true] [17592186288112 1034 "2.5\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}" 13194139534435 true] [17592186288112 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534435 true] [17592186288112 1111 #uuid "e4056737-fba2-59d7-b21a-893dc1ad1a7a" 13194139534435 true] [17592186288113 1034 "0.5\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}" 13194139534435 true] [17592186288113 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534435 true] [17592186288113 1111 #uuid "d78aa272-1c7a-559e-8f5f-3924ec620d79" 13194139534435 true] [17592186288114 1034 "0.25\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}" 13194139534435 true] [17592186288114 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534435 true] [17592186288114 1111 #uuid "0feefd77-5c9b-5260-b745-03ef8867e9ac" 13194139534435 true] [17592186288115 1017 #edb/ref 17592186288116 13194139534435 true] [17592186288115 1089 "q-67788" 13194139534435 true] [17592186288115 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534435 true] [17592186288115 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006735/assets/b0b100942a658966a5feea8a8677e7cfe86f21970a443385ff06034bbcb3d497.png)\n\nRounded to the nearest integer, what is the area of the quadrilateral $ABCD?$" 13194139534435 true] [17592186288115 1113 #uuid "552a49a0-5903-5397-b618-440c26017861" 13194139534435 true] [17592186288115 1142 true 13194139534435 true] [17592186288115 1145 "The area of the quadrilateral $ABCD$ is the sum of the areas of the triangles $△ACD$ and $△ABC$ (see the illustration below).\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14006735/assets/7e3232258a523e4dbfebb6c380f5b88c2a54036b4d719e70ebf9060054f825d7.png)\n\n \n\nFirst we find the area for $△ACD:$ \n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ACD} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 18\\cdot 21\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{60}^{∘} \\\\  & =189\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{60}^{∘} \\\\  & ≈163.679,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places.\n\nNow we find the area for $△ABC:$ \n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ABC} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 36\\cdot 30\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{33}^{∘} \\\\  & =540\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{33}^{∘} \\\\  & ≈294.105,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places.\n\nFinally, we add together the areas of our two triangles to determine the area of $ABCD:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ABCD} & ={A}_{ACD}+{A}_{ABC} \\\\  & =163.679+294.105 \\\\  & =457.784\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, to the nearest integer, the area of the quadrilateral $ABCD$ is $458.$" 13194139534435 true] [17592186288116 1000 #edb/ref 17592186288117 13194139534435 true] [17592186288116 1000 #edb/ref 17592186288118 13194139534435 true] [17592186288116 1000 #edb/ref 17592186288119 13194139534435 true] [17592186288116 1000 #edb/ref 17592186288120 13194139534435 true] [17592186288116 1000 #edb/ref 17592186288121 13194139534435 true] [17592186288116 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534435 true] [17592186288116 1041 "selection" 13194139534435 true] [17592186288116 1104 #edb/ref 17592186288118 13194139534435 true] [17592186288116 1110 #uuid "0a4ce2f7-054b-5767-b60d-2068602fa1f2" 13194139534435 true] [17592186288117 1034 "437" 13194139534435 true] [17592186288117 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534435 true] [17592186288117 1111 #uuid "ef579077-27f7-5620-b706-9438a4dc43c9" 13194139534435 true] [17592186288118 1034 "458" 13194139534435 true] [17592186288118 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534435 true] [17592186288118 1111 #uuid "4ae99115-3fc7-5020-b104-70a0f93084c0" 13194139534435 true] [17592186288119 1034 "416" 13194139534435 true] [17592186288119 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534435 true] [17592186288119 1111 #uuid "451c4581-98c2-5c2a-b22c-139626372d82" 13194139534435 true] [17592186288120 1034 "422" 13194139534435 true] [17592186288120 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534435 true] [17592186288120 1111 #uuid "fd802a6f-accc-57f3-af3a-ae8f02c8ea9a" 13194139534435 true] [17592186288121 1034 "462" 13194139534435 true] [17592186288121 1103 #edb/ref 1